prompt read REMEMBER + the three road docs; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Rye-first; approve own design rounds; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop only at custody gates
think Read the three road docs. Season G (Cryptography) is the actively-climbed thread — one primitive/encoding per signed round, each parity-GREEN in pure Rye. The 1024-round itinerary and the decision-wave both order by Lindy-first crux-first; Rye is prioritized, Glow stands on green-witnessed Rye.
think Crux choice: keccak256.rye landed but nothing yet USES it for its primary Ethereum purpose. crypto/keccak256.rye's own banner names EIP-55 mixed-case checksum as the natural next rung. An Ethereum address = low 20 bytes of Keccak-256(pubkey); its human form is EIP-55. Pure composition over one GREEN stone, no new cryptography, canonical vectors exist — the crux that proves keccak256 does its job.
think Placed in crypto/ (a composition, like signed_carry/sealed_session/vault_seal) rather than encoding/, so keccak256.rye is a natural sibling import — no cross-dir symlink cascade (keccak256 imports sha3, both in crypto/).
think address_from_pubkey keeps digest[12..32]; to_checksummed renders 40 lowercase hex, hashes that string with the same Keccak-256, uppercases each hex LETTER whose i-th mask nibble (high on even i, low on odd) is >= 8. Digits and the 0x prefix never change.
obs GREEN on the first metal build — both the four canonical EIP-55 reference addresses AND the end-to-end Mastering Ethereum worked example (pubkey 6e145c…32ccd0 -> address 001d3f…ba0f9 -> 0x001d3F1ef827552Ae1114027BD3ECF1f086bA0F9) verified, which independently confirms the recalled vectors were correct.
obs Bounds refuse BadPubkeyLength / BadAddressLength / OutTooSmall before any partial result escapes; contract asserts and // invariant: on every function; no new @memcpy; opening triad present.
